  "summary": "Prepare the approved 0.14.0 release without changing the standalone Assent stage.",
  "why": "Luis approved 0.14.0 and a one-time native-Git push/tag exception. Version metadata, runtime status, README, status documentation and changelog now agree; ontology bytes and stage 8c are unchanged. Two release-claim RED tests fail on 0.13.3; 14 status/milestone tests pass after the change. The clean 815ed63b baseline completed with 3338 passed, 11 failed, 3 skipped; all failures were the producer binding repaired at 0af43640. The 22-test corrected document path preserves both old executions. This transaction selects existing full/docs/package gates and the configured tag-triggered publisher, not new dependencies or a stable wire. Actual push, tag, remote tests and PyPI publication remain to be observed. Uncommitted paper/research work and the in-progress undesired-observation integration are excluded.",
